  <ThingDef ParentName="JJK_PuppetRaceBase"><defName>JJK_CursedCorpseDoll</defName><label>cursed corpse doll</label><description>A crafted doll animated by a single cursed-energy core, inspired by Yaga's ordinary cursed corpses. It guards against nearby enemies and can follow its maker. It is an object, not a cursed spirit or resurrected person: it cannot be absorbed by Cursed Spirit Manipulation. It runs independently until its finite charge is exhausted, even if its maker is incapacitated. Standby conserves charge. Repair kits repair damage; its core cannot be resurrected after destruction.</description><comps><li Class="JJKMod.CompProperties_CursedCorpse"/><li Class="JJKMod.CompProperties_AnimalCorpseAppearance"/></comps></ThingDef>
  <ThingDef ParentName="JJK_PuppetRaceBase"><defName>JJK_MechamaruPuppet</defName><label>mechamaru puppet</label><description>A mechanical cursed corpse controlled remotely through Puppet Manipulation. Its controller must be conscious and on this map, but need not be mobile. Control fails during technique sealing, burnout or Domain Amplification. The core stores up to 120 charge, drains 0.5 every 250 active ticks, and powers its attacks. Auto-fire uses Ultra Cannon; direct orders are available on the puppet or controller. Ultimate Cannon requires a Grade 1 controller and can harm allies near the impact. This is the standard puppet, not Mode: Absolute.</description><statBases><ArmorRating_Sharp>0.45</ArmorRating_Sharp><ArmorRating_Blunt>0.35</ArmorRating_Blunt></statBases><race><baseHealthScale>2</baseHealthScale></race><comps><li Class="JJKMod.CompProperties_CursedCorpse"><mech>true</mech></li></comps></ThingDef>
  <PawnKindDef><defName>JJK_CursedCorpseDoll_Kind</defName><label>cursed corpse doll</label><race>JJK_CursedCorpseDoll</race><combatPower>100</combatPower><lifeStages><li><bodyGraphicData><texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Bear/Bear</texPath><graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass><drawSize>2.7</drawSize><color>(112,82,65)</color></bodyGraphicData></li></lifeStages></PawnKindDef>
  <PawnKindDef><defName>JJK_Mechamaru_Kind</defName><label>mechamaru puppet</label><race>JJK_MechamaruPuppet</race><combatPower>260</combatPower><lifeStages><li><bodyGraphicData><texPath>JJK/Presentation/Mechamaru</texPath><graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass><drawSize>1.6</drawSize></bodyGraphicData></li></lifeStages></PawnKindDef>
  <ResearchProjectDef><defName>JJK_CursedCorpseConstruction</defName><label>cursed corpse construction</label><description>Build single-core cursed corpses and repair kits at the cursed materials bench. Any sorcerer can activate an ordinary doll. Mechamaru shells require the innate Puppet Manipulation gene to activate. Research does not grant this gene or create self-sustaining three-core people.</description><tab>JJK_Jujutsu</tab><prerequisites><li>JJK_CursedMaterialsRefinement</li><li>JJK_SorcererTraining</li></prerequisites><baseCost>2400</baseCost><techLevel>Industrial</techLevel><researchViewX>3</researchViewX><researchViewY>2.4</researchViewY></ResearchProjectDef>
  <JobDef><defName>JJK_RechargePuppet</defName><driverClass>JJKMod.JobDriver_RechargePuppet</driverClass><reportString>Recharging a cursed corpse.</reportString></JobDef>
  <JobDef><defName>JJK_RepairPuppet</defName><driverClass>JJKMod.JobDriver_RepairPuppet</driverClass><reportString>Repairing a cursed corpse.</reportString></JobDef>
  <GeneDef ParentName="JJK_CTGeneBase"><defName>JJK_CT_Gene_PuppetManipulation</defName><label>puppet manipulation</label><description>An innate technique for controlling cursed corpse puppets remotely. Grants Ultra Cannon, Ultra Spin, Ultra Shield, Boost On, Ultimate Cannon and Remote Recharge orders for constructed Mechamaru puppets. Craft and activate shells first. One bound construct is allowed at Grades 4-3, two at Grades 2-1 and three at Special/Calamity; ordinary dolls share this limit. Same-map control is a gameplay adaptation: Kokichi's exceptional national range came from his Heavenly Restriction. This gene does not impose that restriction.</description><iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/CT_SpiritManipulation</iconPath><displayOrderInCategory>210</displayOrderInCategory><modExtensions><li Class="TaranMagicFramework.AbilityExtension"><abilityTrees><li>JJK_CT_PuppetManipulation</li></abilityTrees><countAsActive>true</countAsActive></li></modExtensions></GeneDef>
  <TaranMagicFramework.AbilityTreeDef><defName>JJK_CT_PuppetManipulation</defName><label>puppet manipulation</label><unlockedByDefault>false</unlockedByDefault></TaranMagicFramework.AbilityTreeDef>
  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase"><defName>JJK_DollShell</defName><label>cursed corpse doll shell</label><description>An unanimated physical puppet. A sorcerer can activate it for 30 CE, consuming the shell to create a bound construct with 60 of 120 core charge. Ordinary sorcerers may bind one; Puppet Manipulation increases the total to two at Grade 2 and three at Special. Select the construct for standby and follow controls. Right-click it with a sorcerer to recharge: 30 CE adds 60 charge when the core holds no more than 60.</description><graphicData><texPath>Things/Item/Resource/ComponentIndustrial</texPath><graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass><color>(0.7,0.45,0.8)</color></graphicData><statBases><MaxHitPoints>100</MaxHitPoints><MarketValue>500</MarketValue><Mass>8</Mass><WorkToMake>3000</WorkToMake></statBases><stackLimit>1</stackLimit><thingCategories><li>Items</li></thingCategories><costList><Cloth>50</Cloth><Steel>30</Steel><JJK_CursedResidue>30</JJK_CursedResidue></costList><recipeMaker><workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat><workSkill>Crafting</workSkill><recipeUsers><li>JJK_CursedMaterialsBench</li></recipeUsers><researchPrerequisite>JJK_CursedCorpseConstruction</researchPrerequisite><skillRequirements><Crafting>6</Crafting></skillRequirements></recipeMaker><comps><li Class="CompProperties_Usable"><useJob>UseItem</useJob><useLabel>Animate {0_label}</useLabel><useDuration>300</useDuration></li><li Class="JJKMod.CompProperties_ActivatePuppet"><kind>JJK_CursedCorpseDoll_Kind</kind><mech>false</mech></li></comps></ThingDef>
  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase"><defName>JJK_MechamaruShell</defName><label>mechamaru shell</label><description>An unanimated physical puppet. A Puppet Manipulation sorcerer can activate it for 30 CE, consuming the shell to create a bound construct with 60 of 120 core charge. Ordinary sorcerers may bind one; Puppet Manipulation increases the total to two at Grade 2 and three at Special. Select the construct for standby and follow controls. Right-click it with a sorcerer to recharge: 30 CE adds 60 charge when the core holds no more than 60.</description><graphicData><texPath>Things/Item/Resource/ComponentIndustrial</texPath><graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass><color>(0.7,0.45,0.8)</color></graphicData><statBases><MaxHitPoints>100</MaxHitPoints><MarketValue>1400</MarketValue><Mass>25</Mass><WorkToMake>6000</WorkToMake></statBases><stackLimit>1</stackLimit><thingCategories><li>Items</li></thingCategories><costList><Steel>120</Steel><ComponentIndustrial>4</ComponentIndustrial><JJK_CursedSteel>30</JJK_CursedSteel><JJK_CursedResidue>60</JJK_CursedResidue></costList><recipeMaker><workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat><workSkill>Crafting</workSkill><recipeUsers><li>JJK_CursedMaterialsBench</li></recipeUsers><researchPrerequisite>JJK_CursedCorpseConstruction</researchPrerequisite><skillRequirements><Crafting>8</Crafting></skillRequirements></recipeMaker><comps><li Class="CompProperties_Usable"><useJob>UseItem</useJob><useLabel>Animate {0_label}</useLabel><useDuration>300</useDuration></li><li Class="JJKMod.CompProperties_ActivatePuppet"><kind>JJK_Mechamaru_Kind</kind><mech>true</mech></li></comps></ThingDef>
  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase"><defName>JJK_PuppetRepairKit</defName><label>cursed corpse repair kit</label><description>Select a colonist and right-click an allied damaged cursed corpse to repair it. The colonist carries one kit to the puppet and works for 300 ticks. Consumes one kit to repair 30 injury damage OR restore one missing part. Cannot resurrect a destroyed core.</description><graphicData><texPath>Things/Item/Resource/ComponentIndustrial</texPath><graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass><color>(0.7,0.45,0.8)</color></graphicData><statBases><MaxHitPoints>100</MaxHitPoints><MarketValue>90</MarketValue><Mass>1</Mass><WorkToMake>900</WorkToMake></statBases><stackLimit>10</stackLimit><thingCategories><li>Items</li></thingCategories><costList><Steel>15</Steel><JJK_CursedResidue>5</JJK_CursedResidue></costList><recipeMaker><workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat><workSkill>Crafting</workSkill><recipeUsers><li>JJK_CursedMaterialsBench</li></recipeUsers><researchPrerequisite>JJK_CursedCorpseConstruction</researchPrerequisite><skillRequirements><Crafting>4</Crafting></skillRequirements></recipeMaker></ThingDef>
  <HediffDef><defName>JJK_PuppetShield</defName><label>ultra shield</label><description>Temporary puppet enhancement for 600 ticks. IncomingDamageFactor multiplied by 0.55.</description><hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass><isBad>false</isBad><initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity><comps><li Class="HediffCompProperties_Disappears"><disappearsAfterTicks>600</disappearsAfterTicks></li></comps><stages><li><statFactors><IncomingDamageFactor>0.55</IncomingDamageFactor></statFactors></li></stages></HediffDef>
  <HediffDef><defName>JJK_PuppetBoost</defName><label>boost on</label><description>Temporary puppet enhancement for 600 ticks. MoveSpeed multiplied by 1.4.</description><hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass><isBad>false</isBad><initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity><comps><li Class="HediffCompProperties_Disappears"><disappearsAfterTicks>600</disappearsAfterTicks></li></comps><stages><li><statFactors><MoveSpeed>1.4</MoveSpeed></statFactors></li></stages></HediffDef>
